A thousand years ago, the Khmer Empire was very powerful. King Jayavarman the Seventh built many temples and hospitals. Temple builders made beautiful stone carvings. Royal roads connected the ancient city of Angkor with other towns. A clever reservoir system kept water for the rice fields. We can still read an old inscription on the stones.

